{
  "id": "mental-apparatus",
  "term": "mental apparatus",
  "definition": "In Freudian theory, the mental apparatus is the basic organization of mental activity along two main modes: a primary process that tends to form associations and a secondary process that supports perspective-taking. In this framework, primary process thinking is linked especially with the unconscious and dreams, while secondary process thinking follows more reflective rules.",
